For every change i ask you, if we are not in the *main* or *develop* branches, you should commit and push it to the distant branch. Do not be complicated, just :
- git add .
- commit -m "<Your custom message>"
- git push

In case of error during the push, try git push --set-upstream origin <branch>. If it does not work after this, do not go further. If it is possible, in addition of the title, add a description of your changes that can be usefull for the other maintainers of the project.